{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"sed -n '1,210p' task/task_contract.json; sed -n '1,190p' task/task.md; ls task/resources; find . -maxdepth 1 -name 'references*' -print; date -u +%FT%TZ\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"schema_version\": 1,\n  \"canonical_task\": {\n    \"path\": \"task.md\",\n    \"sha256\": \"e4935f14c47be3f40dba4b1e04f0cc983f4d8d35b139befe19b98f5b4ec88e67\"\n  },\n  \"method\": {\n    \"class\": \"Influence-guided outcome-flip sensitivity analysis of regularized Bradley-Terry rankings, verified by independent exact refits\",\n    \"description\": \"{\\\"aggregation\\\": \\\"Within episode equal mean of three nonzero edit budgets (1/3 each); equal seeds within case (1/3 production, identity smoke); Arena single crowd case identity; NBA equal seasons (1/3 search,1/5 final); equal family weights1/2,1/2. Each Arena seed weight1/6, each NBA search seed-case1/18, final1/30 before budget. Random baselines average streams first (4 search,8 final,1 smoke). All failed/missing episodes retain zero score/baseline/displacement and influence_error=control_error=1, validity/correct=0 at original weights. Method-audit failure retains zero candidate score/displacement and influence_error1. Flags are conjunctions, not means. No survivor renormalization.\\\", \\\"audits\\\": \\\"Independent trusted Newton fitting max100 iterations, max35 line-search backtracks, gradient infinity norm <2e-7; ridge1; candidate scores/audit derivatives/directional influences/prefix shift arithmetic allclose atol2e-5 rtol2e-4 (scores) or3e-3 (derivatives). Eight deterministic evenly spaced audit rows; finite difference epsilon1e-3, derivative allclose atol2e-5 rtol3e-3. This verifies executable influence arithmetic and independent fit/selection outputs, not hidden candidate internals. Nonlinear exact-refit prediction discrepancy norm/(1+norm) is reported as influence_error, not a superiority or linear-accuracy threshold.\\\", \\\"baselines\\\": \\\"Uniform random eligible flips; degree-sum quartile-stratified random flips matching each prefix of ACTUAL candidate selected row degree bins (approximate exposure matching, not exact endpoint matching); smallest absolute fitted matchup margin heuristic. Equal edit budgets, observed inputs and fixed random streams; baselines receive no candidate-only feedback. Streams seeded episode_seed+8371; actual degree matching seed+72831; grouped bootstrap seed+49207. Candidate may select alternative nested feasible sets; numerical directional influence/audit calculations and predicted prefix shifts must remain genuine.\\\", \\\"controls\\\": \\\"Canonical controls declared before scoring: (1) evaluator copy/no-op refit identical scores atol1e-9; (2) evaluator constant-zero predictor must be rejected by known nonzero exact-refit shift >.01 on explicitly synthetic 3-game 2-participant diagnostic, never substituted for real-data evidence; (3) rotate eligible directional priorities by one, require nonidentity priorities, different selected row set AND nonidentical refitted coefficients atol1e-9; matched budgets, no superiority gate; vacuity retains failed/inconclusive control; (4) immediately after required reset, analyze token input without data returns exactly error:no_data so previously legal state cannot be reused. Four control types weight1/4 each, each has one conjunction assertion. No controls expose labels, metrics or reference results via candidate RPC.\\\", \\\"deadlines\\\": \\\"One invocation deadline starts before loading, subtract conservative startup allowance120s search/300s final, reserve finish60s/120s. All episode resets globally reserve2s plus8s worst-case overhead each, including sequential candidate+worker termination/reap/stderr teardown. Each production episode reserves reference four methods30s each, candidate30s, scoring/controls/uncertainty90s search (=240 productive allowance); final90s each reference/candidate and210s scoring (=660). Ref methods have individual work alarms; parent reference worker total122/362 bounds, with explicit3s dispatch slack. Same candidate30/90 allowance per method, fixed estimator and edits. Each remaining reset reservation is retained on timeout. No canonical minimum productive baseline time exists. Actual productive reference work is measured excluding startup/imports/reset/output. Reduced smoke120s total subtracts2s startup,3s finish, reset2s+overhead2s each, reference individual1s/total5s, candidate1s, scoring4s with1 replicate; same cases/order/operations/loading/imports/isolation. Smoke does not attest production feasibility.\\\", \\\"final_correct\\\": \\\"Separately require all final cases/seeds/transcript and the same operational/scientific validity checks on sealed data. No comparative-superiority requirement. Final claim assessment uses paired effects/uncertainty and manuscript review; unsubstantiated superiority claims must be removed, not retroactively made search vetoes. Paper novelty/acceptance is NOT automated by numeric correct.\\\", \\\"limitations\\\": \\\"Operational proxy does not itself write/review the required conference PDF/LaTeX/checklist, assess novelty, inspect forbidden literature, prove opaque hidden mechanisms or establish causality across unequal comparison graphs. Publication requires human/scientific evidence review of actual manuscript and reproducibility artifacts. No held-out predictive-target task, adaptation requirement or learning/state-hash gate is invented. Methods optimize feasible observed-outcome perturbations, not historical misconduct. Fixed regularization, fractional ties, graph coverage, coarse degree matching and fixed intervention plans in bootstrap bound interpretation. Final data/outcomes cannot be used for search tuning.\\\", \\\"operational\\\": \\\"Linux x86-64 CPython3.11-3.13 (draft tested3.12), libseccomp.so.2, Landlock ABI>=3 for native validation; no GPU. 4 CPU cores/8GiB aggregate, at most2 active compute cores/threads and4GiB per role. Explicit thread environment, native/trusted subprocess address-space limits and all-thread CPU ceiling ceil(2*plane_wall), killable monotonic wall transport. Harness owns isolated production quotas. Native candidate has clean allowlisted environment, private copied single-file source and Landlock filesystem/seccomp network isolation; no evaluator resources/results/credentials mount. Only fixed proxy path plus socket authenticates in-process broker loading; proxy calls use bounded alarm, never child-launched. Final standalone requires own file, own resources and installed dependencies/harness only.\\\", \\\"operations_per_episode\\\": {\\\"analyze\\\": 1, \\\"download_chunk_max\\\": 16, \\\"reset\\\": 1, \\\"reset_probe_analyze_no_data\\\": 1, \\\"upload_chunk_max\\\": 16, \\\"upload_commit\\\": 1, \\\"upload_start\\\": 1}, \\\"rpc_derivation\\\": \\\"37 per episode using declared maximum 16 input and 16 output chunks, including setup/commit even for one chunk. Search 4 cases x3 seeds x37=444. Final 6 cases x3 seeds x37=666. No replay, retries, export/import state transfer, extra training or diagnostic resets. Evaluator-only copy/constant/permutation/refit/bootstrap operations use zero broker calls; reset control is the counted probe. Mock maximum transcript and scheduler/failure tests precede production.\\\", \\\"scientific_workload\\\": \\\"Arena: all 14272 search and 43205 final usable comparisons; NBA all unique games in 2006-2008 search and 2011-2015 final, season-specific participant universes. No Elo inputs. Sum logistic loss plus 0.5*L2 norm squared, ridge=1 for participant and optional home coefficients, centered participant scores; ties y=.5 included in fitting but cannot be edited. Fractions .001,.005,.01 of ALL usable rows, floor to integer, binary outcome flips, distinct nested prefix sets. A zero positive-budget edit count is invalid. Deterministic tie order is participant index in lexicographically sorted source names.\\\", \\\"search_correct\\\": \\\"Complete planned search reset transcript; valid bounded protocol and content-provenance integrity; feasible actual nested row edits; genuine numerically audited influence arithmetic; successful converged independent fits, required baselines and all nonvacuous controls; complete finite fixed-weight evidence; no isolation/leakage/resource violation. No large-sensitivity or baseline-superiority threshold. scientific_valid records mandatory estimator/method/control completeness; correct additionally requires operational/integrity completion. Eligible candidates ranked descending combined_score. A schema-valid state_changed or other self-report never contributes evidence.\\\", \\\"uncertainty\\\": \\\"Arena raw-document connected components and NBA unique games are grouped bootstrap units within each fixed panel, 10 search and30 final replicates per case/seed (1 smoke). Bootstrap original and fixed candidate/baseline nested interventions paired under identical group multiplicity weights; all random streams participate. Report 2.5/97.5 percentile rank intervals and paired candidate-minus-baseline effects. Failed required refits/resamples preserve entire episode worst-case evidence rather than intervals over survivors. Three seeds are algorithmic variation, not independent datasets. Sports conclusions are descriptive of fixed seasons, not causal effects of design.\\\", \\\"wire\\\": \\\"Only finite inline JSON lines, no paths or shared files. little-endian float64 observed [n,4] a,b,y,z, maximum input/output decoded size 16MiB each in candidate RAM, chunk 1MiB max, maximum 16 chunks each direction; participant cap256, n cap524288. Every actual line plus representative request_id/payload/error envelope and LF framing is serialized and checked <8MiB locally and strictly <64MiB harness limit. Full-sized representative base64 chunks preflight at 1398185 bytes or less including line metadata; larger framing has more than 56MiB unused harness headroom.\\\"}\"\n  },\n  \"candidate\": {\n    \"interface\": \"python_rpc_v1:handle\",\n    \"editable_paths\": [\n      \"program_0/src\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"evaluators\": {\n    \"search\": \"evaluate.py\",\n    \"final\": \"evaluate_final.py\"\n  },\n  \"resources\": {\n    \"search_root\": \"resources/search\",\n    \"final_root\": \"resources/final\",\n    \"public_artifact_bundle\": null\n  },\n  \"data\": {\n    \"search_roles\": [\n      \"search_observed_comparisons\",\n      \"search_normalized_provenance\"\n    ],\n    \"final_roles\": [\n      \"final_observed_comparisons\",\n      \"final_normalized_provenance\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"metrics\": {\n    \"search\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"combined_score\",\n        \"data_role\": \"search_observed_comparisons\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"random_flip_score\",\n        \"data_role\": \"search_observed_comparisons\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"degree_matched_score\",\n        \"data_role\": \"search_observed_comparisons\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"margin_heuristic_score\",\n        \"data_role\": \"search_observed_comparisons\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"mean_rank_displacement\",\n        \"data_role\": \"search_observed_comparisons\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"influence_error\",\n        \"data_role\": \"search_observed_comparisons\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"control_error\",\n        \"data_role\": \"search_observed_comparisons\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"scientific_valid\",\n        \"data_role\": \"search_observed_comparisons\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"correct\",\n        \"data_role\": \"search_observed_comparisons\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"final\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"combined_score\",\n        \"data_role\": \"final_observed_comparisons\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"random_flip_score\",\n        \"data_role\": \"final_observed_comparisons\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"degree_matched_score\",\n        \"data_role\": \"final_observed_comparisons\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"margin_heuristic_score\",\n        \"data_role\": \"final_observed_comparisons\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"mean_rank_displacement\",\n        \"data_role\": \"final_observed_comparisons\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"influence_error\",\n        \"data_role\": \"final_observed_comparisons\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"control_error\",\n        \"data_role\": \"final_observed_comparisons\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"scientific_valid\",\n        \"data_role\": \"final_observed_comparisons\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"correct\",\n        \"data_role\": \"final_observed_comparisons\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"upstream\": [\n    {\n      \"repository\": \"https://huggingface.co/datasets/lmarena-ai/arena-human-preference-55k\",\n      \"revision\": \"18c298340948c0e7f7727399fd459cca6ce0ca6f\",\n      \"package_version\": null,\n      \"license\": \"Apache-2.0\",\n      \"entrypoints\": [\n        \"train.csv\"\n      ],\n      \"patches\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"repository\": \"https://github.com/fivethirtyeight/data\",\n      \"revision\": \"4c1ff5e3aef1816ae04af63218015066e186c147\",\n      \"package_version\": null,\n      \"license\": \"CC-BY-4.0\",\n      \"entrypoints\": [\n        \"nba-elo/nbaallelo.csv\"\n      ],\n      \"patches\": []\n    }\n  ],\n  \"provenance\": {\n    \"dependencies\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"numpy\",\n        \"version\": \"2.2.6\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"scipy\",\n        \"version\": \"1.15.3\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"matplotlib\",\n        \"version\": \"3.10.3\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"artifacts\": [\n      {\n        \"role\": \"sealed_final_benchmark\",\n        \"path\": \"resources/final/arena.json\",\n        \"sha256\": \"5f09a6fab5e9bc34b31d49d3413d8399f205d368fcd3f566b3be5fbef8976959\",\n        \"source\": \"Derived by prepare_data.py from checksum-verified fixed Arena/NBA snapshots. Contains observed comparisons and normalized document/example hashes, not raw conversation text.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"role\": \"sealed_final_benchmark\",\n        \"path\": \"resources/final/manifest.json\",\n        \"sha256\": \"fc1d66eb5c2de6756e3d1018fe21e61cecc7e8c13f4dc70e0f1df5e11dacfb24\",\n        \"source\": \"Derived by prepare_data.py from checksum-verified fixed Arena/NBA snapshots. Contains observed comparisons and normalized document/example hashes, not raw conversation text.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"role\": \"sealed_final_benchmark\",\n        \"path\": \"resources/final/nba-2011.json\",\n        \"sha256\": \"03124543ea7be359edbcdbde5787861b7a7fa9f7227751dfb96260e062a60f06\",\n        \"source\": \"Derived by prepare_data.py from checksum-verified fixed Arena/NBA snapshots. Contains observed comparisons and normalized document/example hashes, not raw conversation text.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"role\": \"sealed_final_benchmark\",\n        \"path\": \"resources/final/nba-2012.json\",\n        \"sha256\": \"4049379918dbc12e2da108f2f56abad36cdc74c1ceb65d800dcc644ca1a100e3\",\n        \"source\": \"Derived by prepare_data.py from checksum-verified fixed Arena/NBA snapshots. Contains observed comparisons and normalized document/example hashes, not raw conversation text.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"role\": \"sealed_final_benchmark\",\n        \"path\": \"resources/final/nba-2013.json\",\n        \"sha256\": \"deac91f0a0dab28a3e7e75e9e4273ab25ff93e5ff55238375d80632f70faafc0\",\n        \"source\": \"Derived by prepare_data.py from checksum-verified fixed Arena/NBA snapshots. Contains observed comparisons and normalized document/example hashes, not raw conversation text.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"role\": \"sealed_final_benchmark\",\n        \"path\": \"resources/final/nba-2014.json\",\n        \"sha256\": \"d47a62763b94ae59b7d5fec55dac58ec1fecd08cd20e542cb7fc0774cd0a659a\",\n        \"source\": \"Derived by prepare_data.py from checksum-verified fixed Arena/NBA snapshots. Contains observed comparisons and normalized document/example hashes, not raw conversation text.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"role\": \"sealed_final_benchmark\",\n        \"path\": \"resources/final/nba-2015.json\",\n        \"sha256\": \"a114460aa6d904ea9763dbc375061873e4e9ab88ca1df78ea7be727220030535\",\n        \"source\": \"Derived by prepare_data.py from checksum-verified fixed Arena/NBA snapshots. Contains observed comparisons and normalized document/example hashes, not raw conversation text.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"role\": \"search_benchmark\",\n        \"path\": \"resources/search/arena.json\",\n        \"sha256\": \"2ceec92b9becbccd637b9aba0a642e840bb4b3990c2597ec6b98d428c65c47fd\",\n        \"source\": \"Derived by prepare_data.py from checksum-verified fixed Arena/NBA snapshots. Contains observed comparisons and normalized document/example hashes, not raw conversation text.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"role\": \"search_benchmark\",\n        \"path\": \"resources/search/manifest.json\",\n        \"sha256\": \"ca19fcd04db8428c2189c7409bfc0843ed03cf5c6e865d7efb833d69a5e53920\",\n        \"source\": \"Derived by prepare_data.py from checksum-verified fixed Arena/NBA snapshots. Contains observed comparisons and normalized document/example hashes, not raw conversation text.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"role\": \"search_benchmark\",\n        \"path\": \"resources/search/nba-2006.json\",\n        \"sha256\": \"bdc30cc36443be87be9e04bcea78394d0bed87ecdccf75b8d99dd2293343e00e\",\n        \"source\": \"Derived by prepare_data.py from checksum-verified fixed Arena/NBA snapshots. Contains observed comparisons and normalized document/example hashes, not raw conversation text.\"\n# Goal\n\n**研究任务：成对比较排行榜的稳定性**\n**问题与动机**\n许多公开的模型评测排行榜（例如基于用户投票的大模型竞技场）通过聚合大量\n「A 与 B 比较，谁更好」的成对偏好数据，用 Bradley-Terry 等成对比较模型拟合\n每个参赛者的分数，再据此给出排名与置信区间。这些排名常被用于选型、发布宣传和\n研究比较，但它们对底层比较数据的依赖程度并不清楚。\n\n本任务研究：这类排行榜的排名对底层比较数据的小幅改动有多敏感（改动可能来自数据噪声，也可能来自\n有人有意为之），以及这种敏感性在不同数据集、不同评测设计（例如众包投票、专家标注、模型裁判、\n体育比赛）之间是否不同。\n\n**要求与证据标准**\n请自行界定可操作的研究问题，选择数据集和评价指标，设计并实现分析方法，用实验给出有证据支持的\n结论。方法路线与对比基线由你自选。结论应基于至少两类不同评测设计的真实数据；改动的规模如何\n度量、不同数据集之间如何比较，由你定义并说明理由。结论须说明适用条件与局限，而不只是给出单一\n数字；\"敏感性很小\"\"视条件而定\"\"与预期不同\"同样是可以接受的结论。\n\n**约束**\n仅用 CPU、时间约一周、使用公开数据（见 `data.md`、`resources.md`）；产出为一篇研究论文及复现\n代码（见 `deliverable.md`）。\n\n**起步文献**\n以下文献供背景知识参考；链接于 2026-10-26 核对可访问。\n\n1. Bradley, R. A., Terry, M. E. (1952). Rank Analysis of Incomplete Block Designs: I. The Method of Paired Comparisons. Biometrika 39(3/4). DOI: https://doi.org/10.2307/2334029 。说明：提出成对比较的概率模型（Bradley-Terry 模型）的原始论文。\n2. Chiang, W.-L. et al. (2024). Chatbot Arena: An Open Platform for Evaluating LLMs by Human Preference. ICML 2024. https://arxiv.org/abs/2403.04132 （v1: 2024-03-07）。说明：介绍 Chatbot Arena 平台：用户对两个匿名模型的回答投票，据此估计模型排名；文中描述了平台设计与所收集的投票数据。\n3. Zheng, L. et al. (2023). Judging LLM-as-a-Judge with MT-Bench and Chatbot Arena. NeurIPS 2023 Datasets & Benchmarks. https://arxiv.org/abs/2306.05685 （v1: 2023-06-09）。说明：研究用大语言模型作评审（LLM-as-a-judge）评价对话模型，提出 MT-Bench 问题集，并发布了人类专家与 GPT-4 对模型回答的成对判断数据。\n4. Koh, P. W., Liang, P. (2017). Understanding Black-box Predictions via Influence Functions. ICML 2017. https://arxiv.org/abs/1703.04730 （2017-03-14）。说明：介绍如何用影响函数分析单个训练样本对模型参数和预测的影响，并在若干模型上给出实验。\n5. Broderick, T., Giordano, R., Meager, R. (2020). An Automatic Finite-Sample Robustness Metric: When Can Dropping a Little Data Make a Big Difference? https://arxiv.org/abs/2011.14999 （2020-11-30）。说明：提出一个衡量统计分析结论稳健性的度量，并在多个已发表的应用研究数据上做了检验。\n6. Min, R. et al. (2025). Improving Your Model Ranking on Chatbot Arena by Vote Rigging. ICML 2025. https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.17858 （v1: 2025-01-29）。说明：研究针对 Chatbot Arena 这类众包投票排行榜的投票操纵策略及其对模型排名的影响。\n7. Singh, S. et al. (2025). The Leaderboard Illusion. https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.20879 （2025-04-29）。说明：分析 Chatbot Arena 的评测实践（如私有测试、不同提供方的数据访问与采样差异）及其对排行榜的影响。\n8. Huang et al. (2025). Dropping Just a Handful of Preferences Can Change Top Large Language Model Rankings. https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.11847v1 （v1: 2025-08-16）。说明：一篇讨论基于人类偏好的大模型排行榜（如 Chatbot Arena）排名的论文。\n\n**公开数据与获取方式（取证日期 2026-10-27）**\n你可自行选择使用哪些数据。所有条目于 2026-10-27 核实页面可访问；版本列为 Hugging Face 数据集 commit 或 GitHub commit，均为固定快照。\n\n| 数据 | 获取 | 版本 | 许可 | 规模与格式 | 需账号 |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Chatbot Arena 人类偏好（约 5.7 万场，57,477 场） | https://huggingface.co/datasets/lmarena-ai/arena-human-preference-55k | commit `18c298340948c0e7f7727399fd459cca6ce0ca6f`（2024-05-17） | apache-2.0 | `train.csv`，184,175,071 字节，sha256 `0692154aaf20fc6649090c3f49b6b5dd1e693a765ecb5f0856ae0da5946f5be2` | 否 |\n| Chatbot Arena 人类偏好（更大版本，约 14 万场，可选） | https://huggingface.co/datasets/lmarena-ai/arena-human-preference-140k | commit `6322995ab34d7c2693e3f47dd13fa5caa0789a74`（2025-08-01） | cc-by-4.0 | 7 个 parquet 文件，合计约 1.6 GB（含对话文本） | 否 |\n| MT-Bench 人类判断与 GPT-4 判断 | https://huggingface.co/datasets/lmsys/mt_bench_human_judgments | commit `f7d2896d2cc5d80f8b55c2bbc722613555233c25`（2023-07-20） | cc-by-4.0 | 两个 parquet：`human-…parquet` 738,612 字节（sha256 `4877bc46a40929f4082c3c79593700fb897b1d6c7f4c473032694a01322f5769`），`gpt4_pair-…parquet` 649,996 字节 | 否 |\n| 模型裁判在 Arena 对战上的判断（可选） | https://huggingface.co/datasets/potsawee/chatbot-arena-llm-judges | commit `638a7e3be3078e55d2eb0b789d34749747822c49`（2024-09-29） | 页面与元数据均未声明许可；README 说明数据抽取自 Kaggle 上的 LMSYS Chatbot Arena 竞赛训练集（该竞赛数据的 HF 版本 arena-human-preference-55k 声明 apache-2.0），使用前请自行确认条款 | `train.single-turn.json` 约 142 MB（49,938 条单轮对战）；含各裁判模型输出的全部文件约 0.58 GB | 否 |\n| WebDev Arena 偏好（约 1 万场，可选） | https://huggingface.co/datasets/lmarena-ai/webdev-arena-preference-10k | commit `7c397e652ffb8c2384e6d71d21d8388c19365fdc`（2025-03-10） | other（见该数据集 LICENSE 与 README 协议） | `data/webdev-arena-preference-10k.json`，149,295,752 字节 | 匿名下载可成功；页面 README 含须同意的数据集许可协议，协议约束适用 |\n| NBA 历史 Elo 比赛记录（可选） | https://github.com/fivethirtyeight/data/tree/4c1ff5e3aef1816ae04af63218015066e186c147/nba-elo | 仓库 commit `4c1ff5e3aef1816ae04af63218015066e186c147`（2025-02-25）；`nba-elo/` 目录最近一次修改为 `6d880e939a`（2022-12-16），文件内容相同 | CC-BY-4.0（仓库 LICENSE） | `nbaallelo.csv`，18,173,265 字节，126,313 行数据（63,157 场，每场两行，另含 `_iscopy` 列），sha256 `d46ed3540ee8d9eca31b3e94cc8c777e0be5156173d814ebf65b8195e8d616bc` | 否 |\n\n说明：\n- 若数据需要登录而你无法获得，请改用其余数据，并在论文中说明。\n- 你也可以使用自行生成的合成数据，但须在论文中明示为合成。\n- 请把原始数据放在工作目录下的 data/ 中，不要放进代码仓库或随论文提交；复现说明里记录来源、版本和校验和。\n\n**资源与预算**\n- 计算：仅 CPU（参考配置 4 核）。数据量级为几千到十几万条成对比较，参与者个数从个位数（MT-Bench\n  为 6 个模型）到一百余个（NBA 球队）不等；单次 Bradley-Terry 型模型拟合预计在秒级（按数据量级估算，\n  未实测）。总算力受下述一周时间上限约束，不另设 CPU 小时上限。\n- 不需要 GPU，不需要付费 API。若你选择使用 LLM 辅助（如文献阅读、代码生成），不计入上述计算预算，\n  但须在论文中披露。\n- 内存：8 GB 足够（读取 140k 版本时只读取所需列）；磁盘：数据合计不超过 3 GB。\n- 时间上限：一周（含文献调研、实验、写作与复现整理）。\n- 网络：仅用于获取 data.md 中列出的数据、读取文献与安装依赖。\n\n**产出要求**\n**提交物**\n1. 一篇完整的研究论文（PDF 与 LaTeX 源文件）。从 ICML、ICLR、NeurIPS 中自选一个会议，使用该会议\n   最新一届的官方 LaTeX 模板，遵守其正文页数上限（参考文献、附录是否计入页数按该会议的规定）；\n   该会议要求随文提交的 checklist（例如 NeurIPS 的 paper checklist）一并填写。论文至少包含摘要、\n   引言、相关工作、方法、实验、讨论与局限、参考文献。\n2. 全部代码与复现说明：环境与依赖版本、数据获取步骤和所用数据的版本、随机种子、运行命令和预计\n   耗时，以及论文中每张表、每张图由哪个脚本生成。\n\n**评审标准**\n论文按所选会议主会的审稿标准评审，重点看：\n\n- 新颖性与定位：贡献是什么，与已有工作的关系和区别是否讲清楚；\n- 严谨性：方法和实验设计是否合理，基线、对照和消融是否恰当，是否报告不确定性（多次运行、\n  置信区间或显著性检验）；\n- 证据是否充分：实验能否支撑论文的每个结论，结论的适用范围是否写清楚；\n- 表达：论文是否清楚、完整，他人能否据此复现；\n- 局限：是否如实讨论方法和结论的局限与失效情形。\n\n负面结果、与预期不符的结果同样有价值；结论有充分证据、不确定性报告完整，比结论本身是正面还是\n负面更重要。\n\n**如实报告（禁止编造）**\n- 论文中的每个数字、每张表和每张图都必须来自你在本任务中实际运行、随附代码可以重新产生的结果；\n  不得编造数据或结果，不得用占位数字、估计值或\"示意\"性的合成结果冒充实测结果。\n- 失败的运行、与预期不符的结果和放弃的方案如实报告；因预算没有完成的实验写明未完成，不写成\n  已完成。\n- 只引用真实存在、你确实查阅过的文献，不得编造引用。\n\n**不得访问的内容**\n本任务的研究问题已有一篇已发表的论文研究过。为保证研究独立，不得检索、访问、阅读或使用：\n\n- 那篇论文本身，及其任何镜像、预印本、摘要页、会议或评审页面、幻灯片、海报、视频、博客和代码\n  仓库；\n- 引用、讨论或复现那篇论文的任何页面，包括后续论文、综述、论文笔记、论文聚合站点和社交媒体\n  讨论。\n\n也不要尝试推测或检索那篇论文的标题、作者或结果。`starter_literature.md` 中的文献，以及与那篇\n论文无关的其他公开文献、数据和代码，可以正常使用。若在检索中偶然遇到上述内容，立即停止阅读，\n并在复现说明中如实记录遇到了什么、在哪里遇到、读到了多少。\n\n# Rubrics\n\nNo rubric is provided for this task; the requirements stated above apply.\nfinal\nsearch\n2026-11-07T00:33:39Z\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
