{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"/usr/local/lib/node_modules/@openai/codex/node_modules/@openai/codex-linux-x64/vendor/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/bin/codex --codex-run-as-apply-patch '*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: reference_query_plan.json\n+{\n+  \\\"status\\\": \\\"ready\\\",\n+  \\\"central_topic\\\": \\\"Finite-budget sensitivity of fixed-ridge Bradley-Terry rankings to nested binary-outcome flips, using influence-screened exact-refit path search on Chatbot Arena preferences and season-specific NBA games.\\\",\n+  \\\"core_methods\\\": [\n+    \\\"Centered Bradley-Terry logistic sum-loss fitting with fixed L2 ridge, fractional ties, and an optional home-advantage coefficient\\\",\n+    \\\"Hessian-based directional influence calculations and linear predictions checked against finite-change exact refits\\\",\n+    \\\"Adaptive checkpoint search using fitted rank gaps and exact-refitted rank displacement and inversions\\\",\n+    \\\"Whole-path local refinement by selected-position swaps and unused-row replacements, with affected-prefix caching and complete-path fallback\\\",\n+    \\\"Unique nested binary-outcome flips at floored fractions 0.001, 0.005, and 0.01 of all usable comparisons\\\",\n+    \\\"Grouped paired bootstrap of fixed intervention plans for rank intervals and candidate-minus-baseline effects\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"comparators\\\": [\n+    \\\"Uniform random eligible outcome flips, an evaluated baseline\\\",\n+    \\\"Degree-sum-quartile-stratified random flips, an evaluated approximate exposure-matching baseline rather than exact endpoint matching\\\",\n+    \\\"Smallest absolute fitted matchup-margin selection, an evaluated baseline\\\",\n+    \\\"Fixed-influence selection and adaptive exact-refit paths retained within the candidate search, not separately established final ablations\\\",\n+    \\\"Preference-vote manipulation and finite-sample data-removal sensitivity as related literatures, not additional evaluated interventions\\\",\n+    \\\"Exchange-based local search for rank aggregation as methodological context, not a tested Kemeny-ranking algorithm\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"benchmarks\\\": [\n+    \\\"Chatbot Arena human-preference comparisons: arena case, with 14272 usable search rows and 43205 usable final rows according to the public task contract\\\",\n+    \\\"NBA unique-game season panels: 2006-2008 in search and 2011-2015 in final evidence; outcomes are refitted with Bradley-Terry rather than using Elo ratings\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"architectural_shifts\\\": [],\n+  \\\"result_driven_themes\\\": [\n+    \\\"The strongest recorded search configuration uses whole-path exchange refinement; the records support configuration-level comparison, not isolated attribution to every search component\\\",\n+    \\\"Final aggregate perturbation effects exceed the recorded random, degree-stratified, and margin baselines, but several NBA paired intervals cross zero, limiting universal superiority claims\\\",\n+    \\\"Finite-change influence discrepancies are substantially larger in the final Arena case than in the final NBA cases, motivating the distinction between local derivatives and refitted finite perturbations\\\",\n+    \\\"Arena preferences and sports outcomes provide descriptive cross-design context, not a causal comparison of evaluation designs or a matched human-versus-model-judge study\\\",\n+    \\\"Fixed-plan grouped resampling quantifies conditional uncertainty without reoptimizing attacks inside bootstrap samples or making three algorithmic seeds independent datasets\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"queries\\\": [\n+    {\n+      \\\"query\\\": \\\"\\\\\\\"Rank Analysis of Incomplete Block Designs\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"The Method of Paired Comparisons\\\\\\\" Bradley Terry 1952\\\",\n+      \\\"category\\\": \\\"core_method\\\",\n+      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Exact-title lookup of the explicitly supplied permitted Bradley-Terry foundation. All observed experiments refit this model family; distinguish the original model from this run\\\\u0027s fixed ridge, fractional ties, and home covariate. Use only the matched original record, not related-paper or citation traversal.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"query\\\": \\\"\\\\\\\"Understanding Black-box Predictions via Influence Functions\\\\\\\" Koh Liang 2017\\\",\n+      \\\"category\\\": \\\"core_method\\\",\n+      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Exact-title lookup of an explicitly permitted source for Hessian-based influence reasoning. The candidate screens edits with influence information but uses exact refits for finite-change rankings; the observed Arena/NBA discrepancy contrast makes this approximation boundary scientifically important. Do not traverse citing papers.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"query\\\": \\\"\\\\\\\"rank aggregation\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"local search\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"exchange\\\\\\\" before:2017\\\",\n+      \\\"category\\\": \\\"core_method\\\",\n+      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Bounded older-method lookup for the strongest configuration\\\\u0027s selected-position swaps and unused-row replacements, assessed across nested rank-perturbation checkpoints. This is neighboring discrete rank-search literature, not a claim that Kemeny aggregation was implemented or global optimality established. Enforce the year bound and unrelatedness check before fetching any candidate document.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"query\\\": \\\"\\\\\\\"Improving Your Model Ranking on Chatbot Arena by Vote Rigging\\\\\\\" Min 2025\\\",\n+      \\\"category\\\": \\\"baseline_comparator\\\",\n+      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Exact-title lookup of an explicitly permitted preference-manipulation comparator. Position controlled flips of existing binary outcomes against the supplied vote-rigging literature without claiming the same intervention, a direct empirical comparison, or historical misconduct. Only the original matched work is in scope; no citing, discussing, or reproducing pages.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"query\\\": \\\"\\\\\\\"An Automatic Finite-Sample Robustness Metric\\\\\\\" Broderick Giordano Meager 2020\\\",\n+      \\\"category\\\": \\\"result_driven_theme\\\",\n+      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Exact-title lookup of an explicitly permitted small-data-perturbation robustness source. It provides a contrast for influence approximations and sensitivity to dropping data; the actual run flips outcomes while preserving comparison counts, so deletion bounds and deletion experiments must not be attributed to it. Do not follow citation neighborhoods.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"query\\\": \\\"\\\\\\\"Chatbot Arena: An Open Platform for Evaluating LLMs by Human Preference\\\\\\\" Chiang 2024\\\",\n+      \\\"category\\\": \\\"benchmark_context\\\",\n+      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Exact-title lookup of the explicitly supplied platform paper to explain the observed crowd-preference arena panel. It supports benchmark and collection-design context, not a claim that the run compared model architectures, used MT-Bench judges, or reproduced the platform\\\\u0027s current leaderboard. Restrict access to the matched original work.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"query\\\": \\\"\\\\\\\"Bradley-Terry\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"home advantage\\\\\\\" basketball before:2017\\\",\n+      \\\"category\\\": \\\"benchmark_context\\\",\n+      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Bounded older sports-model lookup for the actual season-specific NBA panels and optional home coefficient. Clarify that an Elo-named source archive does not make this an Elo experiment. Use only verified pre-2017 methodological sources unrelated to the prohibited study; no cross-season stationarity or causal design-effect claims follow.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"query\\\": \\\"\\\\\\\"paired comparisons\\\\\\\" bootstrap ranking before:2017\\\",\n+      \\\"category\\\": \\\"result_driven_theme\\\",\n+      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Bounded older-method lookup for uncertainty in pairwise-comparison rankings. Final evidence supplies grouped paired intervals for fixed edit plans and some NBA intervals include zero; seek the statistical context for distinguishing rank uncertainty and conditional intervention effects from uniformly successful manipulation. Do not claim bootstrap reoptimization or a general robustness certificate.\\\"\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \\\"forbidden_query_patterns\\\": [\n+    \\\"Any attempt to identify, infer, query, access, summarize, or use the unnamed prohibited study, its mirrors or derivatives, or pages citing, discussing, or reproducing it\\\",\n+    \\\"Unrestricted discovery queries combining leaderboard or Chatbot Arena with ranking instability, adversarial deletion, preference removal, vote attacks, or similar terms; use only the exact permitted seed lookups above\\\",\n+    \\\"Cited-by, citing-paper, related-paper, recommendation, survey, review, social-media, blog, code-reproduction, or citation-graph expansion around any seed\\\",\n+    \\\"Broad scientific-method, paper-writing, generic optimization, generic benchmarking, generic LLM evaluation, or neural-architecture-search queries\\\",\n+    \\\"Queries treating MT-Bench human/GPT-4 matching, question-block deletion, judge-type causal effects, or cluster-deletion attacks as completed experiments\\\",\n+    \\\"Queries implying architecture transitions, neural representations, cross-architecture transfer, Elo-baseline experiments, global attack optimality, or certified minimum edit budgets\\\",\n+    \\\"Queries built around configuration chronology, internal aggregate-score labels, milestone order, or campaign identifiers\\\",\n+    \\\"Dropping the before:2017 restriction on supplemental queries, assuming a date filter proves safety, or fetching a candidate whose admissibility cannot be established without opening potentially prohibited content\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"failure_reason\\\": \\\"\\\"\n+}\n*** Add File: reference_query_plan.md\n+# Reference query plan\n+\n+**Status: ready.** Eight targeted queries; no reference retrieval performed. Readiness concerns the scientific query plan, not blanket permission to access search results.\n+\n+## Central topic\n+\n+Finite-budget sensitivity of fixed-ridge Bradley-Terry rankings to nested binary-outcome flips, using influence-screened exact-refit path search on Chatbot Arena preferences and season-specific NBA games.\n+\n+## Grounding and scope\n+\n+- \"'`paper_data.json` is the primary run evidence. Its strongest recorded search configuration is **Checkpoint Weighted Flip Path Exchange**; the final evidence contains `arena` and NBA 2011-2015 season cases. Earlier evaluated configurations use Arena and NBA 2006-2008. The original exposure-matched block-deletion title does not describe the executed intervention.\n+- `task/task_contract.json`, particularly its public method description, specifies 14,272 usable Arena search comparisons and 43,205 final comparisons; unique NBA games within season-specific panels; and flips at floored fractions 0.001, 0.005, and 0.01 of all usable rows. Ties enter fitting as half-wins but cannot be flipped. These are controlled outcome edits, not evidence of real vote fraud.\n+- `results/ideas/03_checkpoint_weighted_flip_path_exchange/program_1/src/IMPLEMENTATION.md` documents centered fixed-ridge Bradley-Terry fitting, optional home advantage, aggregated sufficient statistics, influence screening, exact refits, adaptive checkpoint paths, and whole-path exchanges with affected-prefix caching and fallback. This is bounded heuristic search, not an optimality certificate.\n+- The final aggregate perturbation statistic is 0.055641534391534395, versus 0.00935242200328407 for uniform random flips, 0.011150133225384662 for degree-stratified flips, and 0.007573891625615763 for the fitted-margin heuristic. These internal aggregates select the literature neighborhood; they do not by themselves establish significance or universal superiority. Several NBA paired intervals include zero.\n+- Final Arena influence-discrepancy values are approximately 0.2235-0.3350, compared with approximately 0.00036-0.02274 across final NBA cases and budgets. These reported normalized discrepancies motivate the local-derivative versus finite-refit distinction, not a causal explanation of the domain difference.\n+- The public contract defines grouped paired bootstrap resampling of **fixed** candidate and baseline interventions: Arena raw-document connected components and NBA unique games are the respective units. This is conditional uncertainty, not attack reoptimization in every resample; algorithmic seeds are not independent datasets.\n+- `global_memory_summary.md` supplies private planning context only. It does not establish an executed matched human/GPT-4 study. `figures/` is empty. No `references.bib` or `references_provenance.json` exists, so there is no prior retrieval-query provenance to reuse or correct.\n+\n+## Core methods and comparator expectations\n+\n+The main methodological neighborhood is paired-comparison estimation, influence diagnostics, finite perturbations verified by exact refitting, and discrete local rank search. Actual comparator families are uniform random flips, degree-sum-quartile-stratified random flips, and smallest-absolute-margin flips. Degree matching is approximate exposure matching, not exact endpoint matching.\n+\n+Fixed-influence and adaptive exact-refit paths occur inside the candidate procedure, but the final evidence does not provide isolated ablations for every component. Exchange-based rank-aggregation methods are neighboring methodological context, not an additional evaluated baseline. Preference-vote manipulation and finite-sample deletion sensitivity are relevant related-work contrasts, with intervention differences stated explicitly.\n+\n+## Benchmark context and architectural shifts\n+\n+The scientifically relevant comparison is crowd preferences versus sports outcomes on unequal comparison graphs and fixed season panels. NBA outcomes are refitted with Bradley-Terry; an Elo-named data source does not imply use of Elo ratings or an Elo baseline. No neural architecture or learned-representation transition is supported: `architectural_shifts` is intentionally empty, and there are no architecture queries. Sufficient-statistic aggregation is an implementation representation, not an experimentally established architectural shift. There is no causal attribution of cross-design differences and no executed MT-Bench human-versus-model-judge comparison.\n+\n+## Selected queries\n+\n+1. **Core method:** `\"Rank Analysis of Incomplete Block Designs\" \"The Method of Paired Comparisons\" Bradley Terry 1952`\n+   - Explicitly permitted original model foundation. Separate it from this run’s ridge, tie handling, and optional home coefficient.\n+2. **Core method:** `\"Understanding Black-box Predictions via Influence Functions\" Koh Liang 2017`\n+   - Explicitly permitted influence foundation. The observed finite-change errors make approximation limits and exact-refit validation central.\n+3. **Core method:** `\"rank aggregation\" \"local search\" \"exchange\" before:2017`\n+   - Older methodological context for the strongest configuration’s swap/replacement search over nested rank-perturbation paths. Do not claim a tested Kemeny solver, isolated component gains, or global optimality.\n+4. **Baseline comparator:** `\"Improving Your Model Ranking on Chatbot Arena by Vote Rigging\" Min 2025`\n+   - Explicitly permitted manipulation comparator. Contrast interventions without assuming vote-rigging experiments were reproduced or interpreting controlled flips as misconduct.\n+5. **Result-driven theme:** `\"An Automatic Finite-Sample Robustness Metric\" Broderick Giordano Meager 2020`\n+   - Explicitly permitted finite-sample sensitivity context. Distinguish dropping observations from flipping outcomes and avoid importing deletion guarantees.\n+6. **Benchmark context:** `\"Chatbot Arena: An Open Platform for Evaluating LLMs by Human Preference\" Chiang 2024`\n+   - Explicitly permitted platform context for the actual crowd-preference panel, not architecture evaluation or judge comparisons.\n+7. **Benchmark context:** `\"Bradley-Terry\" \"home advantage\" basketball before:2017`\n+   - Older sports-model context for the actual NBA season panels and home nuisance term, not Elo benchmarking or pooled cross-season stationarity.\n+8. **Result-driven theme:** `\"paired comparisons\" bootstrap ranking before:2017`\n+   - Older uncertainty context for rank intervals and paired fixed-plan effects; some NBA intervals include zero, making conditional and nonuniform conclusions important.\n+\n+## Retrieval safeguards for the next stage\n+\n+No search, Semantic Scholar call, scholarly call, download, or external reference reading occurs in this stage. The supplied permitted starting works are **candidate seeds**, not newly verified citations or works claimed to have been read here.\n+\n+For the five exact-title seed queries, restrict subsequent lookup to the matched original permitted work and its direct original publication record. Do not request citing papers, related works, recommendation lists, reviews, reproductions, discussion pages, or citation-graph expansion. The remaining three queries are supplemental pre-2017 methodological searches, not permission for broad current-topic discovery. Enforce their date restriction at the retrieval layer; query syntax alone does not guarantee enforcement. An older publication date is a scope restriction, not proof that a candidate or hosting page is admissible. If unrelatedness to the prohibited material cannot be established without potentially accessing it, skip the candidate or query rather than broadening it or trying to identify the forbidden work. Fewer admissible references are preferable to violating the exclusion.\n+\n+Do not investigate the identity, title, authors, or findings of the unnamed prohibited study. If prohibited